Z||000007||BAM-BAM||06-10-2001||12:14 AM|||| The kit is no longer made. The originator sold one set of molds to an american who had promised to start manufacturing them. As of yet, there have been none sold or even made, to popular knowledge. However, as with all great inventors, there were some backup molds. As I understand it, those molds may (may not) be comming state side as well and hopefully in the hands of a true buisness man. If so, you might see that interior in the not to distant future. There's no gaurentees on that, but the idea has been tossed around. I think it would be awesome and I wouldn't hesitate to buy one if the price is right and color options were made available. That's about all I know. Eddie Snaww I think was the guys name. I really hope that some one saves this interior. BTW, I saw the interior kit for sale on E-Bay a few months back. <P>Peace, B2 OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!<p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 06-10-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000008||Monkeyman||06-10-2001||10:08 AM||||BAM-BAM--You're getting that interior mixed up with another.  Eddy Snaaws interior was MUCH better looking, IMHO.  Eddy did indeed sell his molds to someone around Las Vegas who promised to make them.  Unfortunately, he hasn't produced any.  (Bastard)  I'd buy one of Eddys interiors in a heartbeat.  Here are some pics of Eddys interior.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cool_dash-6_9.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cool_dash-door_4.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/EddySnaauwsdash-gauges_1.jpg"> <P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000009||Scott||06-10-2001||03:34 PM||||Hi guys,<BR>  I've never seen that int. before.  That ROCKS!!!  Who's this Eddy Snaaws guy? When did he make these? Why did he quit?  Now I'm really wishing I woulda kept up w/ Fieros while I was at college.<BR>TIA<BR>Scott ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Predator||06-10-2001||05:05 PM||||That's sharp. I like the Dash and the way the stock guages are aranged. That has to be the best designed interior I have seen for the Fiero. Too bad it's not being made. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Monkeyman||06-10-2001||05:41 PM||||Scott--Eddy is from the Netherlands (did I spell that right?).  He made that dash for himself, then found out that EVERYONE loved the dash.  He produced the molds then sold them to a gentleman here in the States who claimed that he would manufacture the dashes for sale.  So far that hasn't happened.  Eddy didn't want to manufacture the dashes himself (hell of a price for shipping, too).  Hopefully, Eddy has another set of molds lying around that he'd be willing to sell to somebody who really wants to do something for the Fiero community.  If Eddys dash was for sale and I had the money, I'd buy one for sure.<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000012||BAM-BAM||06-10-2001||09:23 PM||||  DOH!!! Your right MM, I did get them confused. Do you know who in Las Vegas bought the molds. I saw them for sale on Ebay a few months ago, I remember posting something about it. It's a shame, I got an E-Mail from Eddy a while back and he seemed rather dissapointed in the fact that he sold the molds and nothing is being made or sold. I hope some one can find the scratch to buy his back ups. I was thinking in that direction but opted to buy some rock bottom utillity stock that will hopefully pay off in the long run. Oh well, Sorry for the confusion  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||BAM-BAM||06-11-2001||12:56 AM||||  Here is a link to the thread that originaly peaked my interest in Eddies interior. Scott Tilden was the name of the guy that bought the molds. Some one said he lived here in Vegas? Just might have to seek him out and plan a midnight rade on the molds. At least talk to him. Anyway I hope this answers some questions. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005493.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005493.html</A> <P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000014||Monkeyman||06-11-2001||06:21 AM||||Yup.  That was him.  Scott Tilden.  I even spoke with him on the phone when he 1st bought the molds.  He said that he wanted to make a couple minor modifications to the mounting hardware, then he'd have them for sale (somewhere around $1500, I think).  I never heard from him again nor has he reponded to my many emails.  My guess is that he's just a spoiled rich kid who wanted his own, one-of-a-kind interior.  "Please, daddy, buy this for me.  Please, please, please!"  If I had the cash (which I don't), I'd buy any of Eddys other molds in a heartbeat.  I'm looking for another job anyway.<P>MM||||reg||1
